# Contributing to {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), [core](docs/agent-governance/core.md),
[architecture](docs/agent-governance/architecture.md),
[planning](docs/agent-governance/planning.md), [testing](docs/quality/testing.md)
and [configuration](docs/operations/configuration.md).

Complete the project-owned [development command map](docs/operations/development.md)
with selected runtimes, native manifests/locks, supported platforms, owners and
actual setup/run/build/test/check commands. Missing product commands remain
unconfigured; document checks cannot substitute for required software execution.
Generated local outputs belong under `artifacts/<tool-or-run>/`; only
`artifacts/README.md` is tracked, and these outputs are not review evidence or
approval.

The starter verifier runs from a separately reviewed source checkout at an exact
immutable commit. It compares common managed bytes and supported structural
records, not product behavior, meaningful local instructions or human approval.
The project contains no Backbone source-history validator, source regression suite
or active source CI. Preserve existing stronger gates during any later adoption.

Keep delivery plans, Task Packets, actual checks, independent reviews and triage
under `docs/changes/<delivery>/`. Run relevant checks, freeze the same base/head/
patch for reviewers and triage before repairs. Before publication, check the actual
committed base/head diff including later evidence commits. A human decides merge,
release and deployment separately. Updates are reviewed changes; no automatic apply.
